# IDK triggers — Infer DevOps Kit

When the user message matches a trigger below, follow **`/IDK`** — **Skill (Dual Resolve — load once):** resolve paths only first — `sicon-infer-devops-kit` → `skills/infer-devops-kit/SKILL.md` (plugin direct → newest `plugins/marketplaces|cache` bounded → user-pack skills dogfood only if no plugin; never prefer pack) — then Read exactly the one resolved file in full. Do **not** Read any other copy of this skill this invoke (if a copy was already loaded this turn, reuse it — this resolve applies from the next invoke).

## Engage when any

- `/IDK <id>` or `/idk <id>` → **recommend**
- `/IDK` or `/idk` (bare — then ask for the card number)
- Clear "infer devops kit" / "IDK" with a card number → **recommend**
- Frozen card / study sheet asking which implement approach → **recommend**
- **Same-thread proceed** after an IDK `Recommendation:` proceed question in this thread: `continue`, `go ahead`, `yes`, `do it`, `proceed`, `ok`, `yep`, or path pin `inline` / `dlb` / `lb` / `devops leading brief` / `superpowers` → **proceed** (dispatch per skill; do not re-classify)
- **Same-thread supply-info** after an IDK `Recommendation: … (fallback)` in this thread: extra context answering the named firm-up items, instead of a proceed answer → **supply info** (re-classify from context per skill; do not dispatch)

**Recommend:** two-line body + `Proceed with <lane>?` question (never `→ continue`). Fallback DLB is labelled `(fallback)`, disclosed as low confidence, and names the specific info that would firm it up; **Continue with recommendation** is always offered, fallback included. **Proceed:** Inline implement / DLB brief / Superpowers per prior Recommendation (user path pin wins). Never stack DLB + Superpowers.

## When NOT to engage

- Casual mention of a work item without asking for an approach pick
- Bare `yes` / `continue` when the last turn was **not** an IDK recommend (other gates, Orient, unrelated asks)
- `/dev-triage`, devops-card creators, or other tools' lanes (unless IDK proceed already dispatched into DLB)
